From 09b305504f8d46d32f7630e18575eb04c208c5ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:35:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.5.0: security hardening pass, defective-fix reworks,
 UI/i18n consolidation

Security review (Phases 1-3) applied to the v2.5.0 tree.

Reworked the five defective fixes from the 2026-08-18 adversarial review:
Gatekeeper binds nw_t.br_ifname (not the tun22/23-overwritten ifname); rtrafd
credits the reply-source (rsrc) for a DNAT'd inbound flow; the Prometheus
staleness bound tracks rtraf_hint with a back-off re-stamp; reaper_fw apply.sh
gained a hard RFWH wrapper so a failed structural hook fails closed (exit 1);
LASTGOOD writes atomically with a completion marker the boot path gates on.

Reverted the QoS priority remap: the defect is real (libtmctl documents
"lower value, lower priority" and the live queues read back inverted) but the
hardware rejects the in-place renumber ("Priority already in use"), so a correct
delqcfg-based fix needs a hardware validation pass. Deferred to a metal session.

New Phase 3 fixes: firewall-object command injection, Warden planted-script RCE,
world-writable working files plus two CSRF endpoints and a constant-time scrape
token, SNMP WAN interface pin and LAN-scoped agentAddress bind, two
DHCP-reservation dnsmasq-injection paths, UPnP PPTP/FTP protect denies, Warden
manual-ban conntrack teardown, rmcp 2FA arming-key lockdown, reaper_export length
cap, httpd Content-Length pre-auth CPU-spin DoS and url[128] OOB, firmware
manifest-injection validation, USB-eject and default-password chpass CSRF tokens,
and rfw_field truncation rule-widening.

Also folds in the shared-escaper (reaper_util.js) consolidation across the Reaper
pages with its i18n dict lockstep, and the tagged-WAN PPPoE-1500 MTU residual.

Build-validated on RT-BE96U (make rt-be96u, MAKE_EXIT=0, "Done! Image 96813GW").
Metal test still pending for the QoS behaviour and the first-boot password flow.
